{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/951816-seeking-counsel-for-an-upcoming-game-i-ll-run","id":951816,"title":"Seeking counsel for an upcoming game i'll run.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-16T10:31:22-07:00","id":951816,"title":"Seeking counsel for an upcoming game i'll run.","content":"Particularly concerning one of my players character.<br /> <br /> So the context first:<br /> I'm running a vampire the requiem set in Miami in the 80s. Since it will be the first vampire game i run i'm keeping it fairly standard in regards with the covenants. Of note is the fact that vampires are finding out that the networks and hooks they've cultivated in mortal society are being subverted, replaced or removed. Tensions are flying high and there are rumors aplenty on who is doing all that. <br /> <br /> As for the character in question:<br /> He is mostly defined by three stats.<br /> 1. He has the merit ressources at 5. The money comes from the characters father, but my player left to me to decide who the father is. I've decided that the father is from old family established in miami from a long time and that presently he is an important politician (state senator or something). He is firmly keeping his son at arms length and basically just gave him money instead of taking care of him. Which leads me to point 2.<br /> 2. He has 1 resolve. Which translated in a pretty severe addiction to drugs. Through which the character's sire met him. <br /> 3. He has 5 intelligence but very few points in mental skills. A good way to represent the character is 'wasted potential' (which i love)<br /> <br /> The character was embraced by a gangrel and, like his sire, joined the carthian tho he is not really active. <br /> <br /> So my concerns are threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. The player didnt put any point in the safe place merit. He argued that with ressources 5 his father paid a place for him. I explained that since he didnt take the merit he was at risk of someone walking in during the day and that people who knows him knows where he lives and he is okay with that.<br /> - Should i have him attribute a few of his points of ressources to temporarily gain the safe place merit???<br /> <br /> Also i was wondering, the rest of my players all took the safe place merit but not the haven merit. Is it wrong???<br /> <br /> 2. The Sire-Childe relationship is predicated on the fact that the sire keeps the character for access to his money. Really the sire would not have embraced him at all but an overdosed forced his hands.<br /> To encourage conflict with the sire i'm thinking of having the player temporarily loses access to some or even all of his ressource merit when, for exemple, the sires takes his credit card for a little bit.<br /> Is that to harsh??? After all the player took that merit to use it and I would be constantly taking it from him (even if only temporarily).<br /> <br /> 3. Finally the fact that ultimately the ressources merit is not in the control of the character makes me feel that eventually there will be a conflict where the character loses his 5 dots of ressources (althought he will be free to reallocate the points elsewhere). I'm just unsure on the best way to approach this. I mean it wouldnt happen at the start of the chronicle but there will come a time when either the characters connection with his family is deemed a threat to the mascarade or something can also happen on the mortal family side of thing to.<br /> So i was wondering if you guys had any idea on what to do with that and also how you dealt with characters losing merits they had while mortal. <br /> <br /> <br /> I appreciate the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:55:35-07:00","id":951835,"title":"","content":"For the Safe Place / Haven issue, I'd allow a no-point build to still be colored by his high resources. I'd make it a fancy-shmancy mortal run condo who's staff is notorious for looking the other way regarding their elite clients' lifestyles. This translates into even the security guards looking the other way unless the police are actively involved. Maybe layer it so that some residents pay a 'premium' to have security, while some residents do not. If the player wants security mechanics, he can buy the merits, OR - I think the Goods/Services section for Equipment Bonuses lists private security guards. He can spend his resources dots as normal to hire one. I'd charge a two-for-one conversion if he wanted to trade Resource for Safe Place dots each Chapter.<br /> <br /> Re: not taking haven - I've seen this as well. Haven is an easy area to skimp on when you are a starting character, and with Safe Place being a speed-bump/requirement for haven, it can seem double expensive compared to other Merits. I've massaged this issue by adding a little oomph to the Haven Merit in my game. Each Kindred has the right of domain in their personal Haven. They only get this right if they've bough the Merit.<br /> <br /> For looking at taking away resources, just make sure to frame it in terms of opportunities. If the player could use some help and hasn't figured out an angle, the Sire could show up looking for money in exchange. No money, no simple solution. Alternatively, if they are buying the Sire as a Mentor, you tend to have to maintain that connection somehow. Cash can be that connection.<br /> <br /> But yes, I think your instinct that consistently taking away a Merit could be harsh is right. Would you arbitrarily take away combat or style Merits from any physical characters? If not, be aware that you're devaluing Mortal Merits from the others. And in this case, it seems something easily written into a background without a mechanical effect. The Sire rescued the Childe to keep that behind-the-scenes cash flowing, and it does, but behind the scenes. Maybe there was even an agreement that the Childe's family trust (once the rich parents are dead) would be turned over whole-hog to the Sire down the road - lots of possibilities.<br /> <br /> Are you worried the Resources merit is going to cause problem for plots down the road?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:57:10-07:00","id":951838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/951816-seeking-counsel-for-an-upcoming-game-i-ll-run#post951816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Particularly concerning one of my players character.<br /> <br /> So the context first:<br /> I'm running a vampire the requiem set in Miami in the 80s. Since it will be the first vampire game i run i'm keeping it fairly standard in regards with the covenants. Of note is the fact that vampires are finding out that the networks and hooks they've cultivated in mortal society are being subverted, replaced or removed. Tensions are flying high and there are rumors aplenty on who is doing all that.<br /> <br /> As for the character in question:<br /> He is mostly defined by three stats.<br /> 1. He has the merit ressources at 5. The money comes from the characters father, but my player left to me to decide who the father is. I've decided that the father is from old family established in miami from a long time and that presently he is an important politician (state senator or something). He is firmly keeping his son at arms length and basically just gave him money instead of taking care of him. Which leads me to point 2.<br /> 2. He has 1 resolve. Which translated in a pretty severe addiction to drugs. Through which the character's sire met him.<br /> 3. He has 5 intelligence but very few points in mental skills. A good way to represent the character is 'wasted potential' (which i love)<br /> <br /> The character was embraced by a gangrel and, like his sire, joined the carthian tho he is not really active.<br /> <br /> So my concerns are threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. The player didnt put any point in the safe place merit. He argued that with ressources 5 his father paid a place for him. I explained that since he didnt take the merit he was at risk of someone walking in during the day and that people who knows him knows where he lives and he is okay with that.<br /> - Should i have him attribute a few of his points of ressources to temporarily gain the safe place merit???<br /> <br /> Also i was wondering, the rest of my players all took the safe place merit but not the haven merit. Is it wrong???<br /> <br /> 2. The Sire-Childe relationship is predicated on the fact that the sire keeps the character for access to his money. Really the sire would not have embraced him at all but an overdosed forced his hands.<br /> To encourage conflict with the sire i'm thinking of having the player temporarily loses access to some or even all of his ressource merit when, for exemple, the sires takes his credit card for a little bit.<br /> Is that to harsh??? After all the player took that merit to use it and I would be constantly taking it from him (even if only temporarily).<br /> <br /> 3. Finally the fact that ultimately the ressources merit is not in the control of the character makes me feel that eventually there will be a conflict where the character loses his 5 dots of ressources (althought he will be free to reallocate the points elsewhere). I'm just unsure on the best way to approach this. I mean it wouldnt happen at the start of the chronicle but there will come a time when either the characters connection with his family is deemed a threat to the mascarade or something can also happen on the mortal family side of thing to.<br /> So i was wondering if you guys had any idea on what to do with that and also how you dealt with characters losing merits they had while mortal.<br /> <br /> <br /> I appreciate the help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh, I'm from Miami! Let me know if I can help at all with setting info.<br /> <br /> I don't have the book in front of me right now (and I can't have it in front of me now) so I won't comment specifically on a particular merit. It does sound like the sire would have, really, just blood-bound the mortal character or turned him into a ghoul, but what's done is done, and I don't think it's appropriate or respectful for you to back out of what you've agreed to. The player is excited about the character they made, and you are the ST, so I think you have to take responsibility for any mistakes you might have made when you said yes.<br /> <br /> Upon reread, this sounded really harsh. I am sorry that I was rude. I sounded callous and uninterested, and I am sorry for that.<br /> <br /> I left it all for posterity, but what I should have said is that as you've already agreed to the character background, you should not turn back and say no now. &quot;Take responsibility&quot; is very rude, and I am sorry that I said that. What I mean by it is to own the decision and move on from it, to take it where it goes and not look back. I do think it was a mistake to agree, but we all make mistakes, and we just have to learn from them and move forward. Saying no to players is hard, but once we say yes, I don't think we should turn back. So I think agreeing to a background where a sire turned this player character only for their money was the wrong decision, but it's done, and I don't think you should take it back. <br /> <br /> To answer your third question, though, remember sanctity of merits--if a character loses a merit they've invested in, the player has those dots to redistribute as they see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  Added my third and fourth paragraph. Upon reread, my post sounded very rude and callous. 08-16-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:59:58-07:00","id":951842,"title":"","content":"Nice to see more people playing Miami games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/951816-seeking-counsel-for-an-upcoming-game-i-ll-run#post951816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The player didnt put any point in the safe place merit. He argued that with ressources 5 his father paid a place for him. I explained that since he didnt take the merit he was at risk of someone walking in during the day and that people who knows him knows where he lives and he is okay with that.<br /> - Should i have him attribute a few of his points of ressources to temporarily gain the safe place merit???</div> </div> </div> </div>He's okay with it as is, so no. If he wants later I'd probably let him move a point in Resources to a point in Safe Place, or just purchase Safe Place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also i was wondering, the rest of my players all took the safe place merit but not the haven merit. Is it wrong??? </div> </div> </div>It's unwise, but that's hardly something to expect from neonates. Haven gives you some added 'mystic' benefits to notice intruders that Safe Place doesn't, but Safe Place is the foundation from which Haven is built upon, being a pre-requisite. Let them purchase it later if they want. If it turns out that, in your game, no one really tries to attack their Safe Place, then they lucked out and didn't need Haven anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. The Sire-Childe relationship is predicated on the fact that the sire keeps the character for access to his money. Really the sire would not have embraced him at all but an overdosed forced his hands.<br /> To encourage conflict with the sire i'm thinking of having the player temporarily loses access to some or even all of his ressource merit when, for exemple, the sires takes his credit card for a little bit.<br /> Is that to harsh??? After all the player took that merit to use it and I would be constantly taking it from him (even if only temporarily). </div> </div> </div>It's not too harsh, it's a common plot hook actually. Keep in mind the Sanctity of Merits, however. Because the character spent 5 Merit dots in Resources, if you take that away, the character should still have access to those 5 Merit dots and can spend them elsewhere, or getting back their Resources, providing there's an in-story justification for it, such as stealing from or killing the sire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Finally the fact that ultimately the ressources merit is not in the control of the character makes me feel that eventually there will be a conflict where the character loses his 5 dots of ressources (althought he will be free to reallocate the points elsewhere). I'm just unsure on the best way to approach this. I mean it wouldnt happen at the start of the chronicle but there will come a time when either the characters connection with his family is deemed a threat to the mascarade or something can also happen on the mortal family side of thing to.<br /> So i was wondering if you guys had any idea on what to do with that and also how you dealt with characters losing merits they had while mortal. </div> </div> </div>Look through the Sanctity of Merits section, it explains it, though you seem to have a grasp of it.<br /> <br /> But conflict is good for storytelling. There's a lot of movies and stories where the rich lose access to their money and have to figure out what to do from there.<br /> <br /> As for how it could work out, a simple way would be having the money be in a trust fund, a common method of wealthy parents keeping their children loaded with cash. But a trust fund is controlled by a lawyer. A vampire, in this case the sire, could simply take control of the lawyer and have them embezzle the money, which would then disappear from records and into the wallet of the sire. They might even be willing to go to jail for it with the Vinculum. A family friend actually did something like this, though he was the lawyer handling the trust funds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:13:21-07:00","id":951851,"title":"","content":"1. No you shouldn't allow resources to function as a safe place. It devalues the merit for the players who did allocate points for safe place. The resources 5 could be an excuse for him to have the merit safe place but it does not afford him the benefits.<br /> <br /> 2. No its not wrong in and of itself as it's storyline material but be judicious in doing so. If you're constantly having him operate at Resources 2 then it would be fair to give him 3 merit points or the attendant xp to spend elsewhere. To reflect the fact that he got good at selling his season passes and movie premiere tickets (skill specialty Scalping) or whatever he does to get by.<br /> <br /> 3. Make it clear he's going to lose part of that merit at the start of the game. When he loses them in the flow of the story, give him the xp at the end of the session to spend or save as he sees fit. If he decides he wants to keep the merit, he should be taking steps in game to either keep the merit or rebuild his fortune on his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:25:18-07:00","id":951859,"title":"","content":"1. In the same way that it is assumed a character with 0 dots of Resources has enough money to keep themselves fed and their bills paid, but has no disposable income beyond that, it is assumed that a character with 0 dots in Safe Place has a roof over their head, but it isn't secured well enough to penalize any attempts to break in. He might have a basic lock on his door or something, but nothing that will really stop a committed trespasser. And having Safe Place but no Haven is fine. Basically, think of Safe Place as how well protected the place is against intrusion - locks, alarms, traps, etc. and Haven as how well suited the place is for a vampire to sleep in. A vampire's Safe Place with 0 dots of Haven is assumed to have a dark corner somehere they can put a coffin in and sleep through the day in without getting ashed, but hasn't been sun-proofed well enough to give them a bonus to rolls to remain awake during the day, and they haven't properly attuned the space to their predatory nature to gain a bonus to Kindred Senses or Perception rolls to notice danger.<br /> <br /> 2. Rather than take Resources dots away, you could have him find that his alloted once-per-chapter 5 dot Availability purchase has already been spent, or that his effective Resources for this month is 4 because his sire overspent. I don't think that's too unreasonable as long as you don't do it all the time.<br /> <br /> 3. Sanctity of Merits pretty much has you covered there. Let's say he is forced to cut ties with his family in the interest of protecting the Masquerade. He might be afforded an extra dot of Clan, Covenant, or City Status as important vampires are more willing to trust him. Or maybe a powerful Carthian admires his decision and decides to act as his Mentor to help ease him more into vampire society. Maybe he keeps his family at arm's length but doesn't want to completely alienate himself from them, so he checks in on them from time to time; he can no longer lay claim to the family fortune, but he's gained a new Touchstone or two. Or, it could be entirely meta and just give him Parkour or something. I wouldn't go that route with it, though. Actually what I would do is let him choose where he wants the Merit dots reallocated to, and ask him to explain how it happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:37:54-07:00","id":951875,"title":"","content":"You could look into Luxury merit of Seers Of The Throne fame. It basically exists to fulfill the role you want it to be: it's cash that's granted to the character from outside source that can and might take it away if you do something that displeases them. You could go for a middle ground here and give him lower dot Luxury (2 dot Luxury is like 5 dot resources anyway), and trade rest of the dots for stuff like Safe Place he wanted to simulate with that cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-16-2016, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:43:40-07:00","id":951880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/951816-seeking-counsel-for-an-upcoming-game-i-ll-run?p=951838#post951838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahhh, I'm from Miami! Let me know if I can help at all with setting info.<br /> <br /> I don't have the book in front of me right now (and I can't have it in front of me now) so I won't comment specifically on a particular merit. It does sound like the sire would have, really, just blood-bound the mortal character or turned him into a ghoul, but what's done is done, and I don't think it's appropriate or respectful for you to back out of what you've agreed to. The player is excited about the character they made, and you are the ST, so I think you have to take responsibility for any mistakes you might have made when you said yes.<br /> <br /> Upon reread, this sounded really harsh. I am sorry that I was rude. I sounded callous and uninterested, and I am sorry for that.<br /> <br /> I left it all for posterity, but what I should have said is that as you've already agreed to the character background, you should not turn back and say no now. &quot;Take responsibility&quot; is very rude, and I am sorry that I said that. What I mean by it is to own the decision and move on from it, to take it where it goes and not look back. I do think it was a mistake to agree, but we all make mistakes, and we just have to learn from them and move forward. Saying no to players is hard, but once we say yes, I don't think we should turn back. So I think agreeing to a background where a sire turned this player character only for their money was the wrong decision, but it's done, and I don't think you should take it back.<br /> <br /> To answer your third question, though, remember sanctity of merits--if a character loses a merit they've invested in, the player has those dots to redistribute as they see fit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome, i'll gather my notes a bit and come back to you with some question regarding miami if you dont mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Tho it may have to wait a bit. <br /> <br /> As for the embraced for the money bit. <br /> We worked on that during the character creation and what happened was more in the line of the sire was delivering drugs, and later vitae to have access to the characters money. But following an overdose the vitae in the body caused a spontaneous embrace (i think its a thing now, if not then the sire took a calculated risk in order to keep the money, not the best move i agree but then hes not known for his great judgment) and the sire is loathe of simply dumping the character because its still easy money for him. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> I love the idea in point 2. After all sanctity of merits can work even on temporary change of points. So if a make the sire take say 2 or 3 ressources then i offer temporarily the appropriate amount of points on something else. I really have to start thinking about that now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Holy i dont think it will pose problem. Actually i'd like, if possible to integrate the ressources to the character development since i feel its an important part of the characters concept. Maybe work on him gaining a sense of responsiblity and using his ressources on communal projet (fits well witht the carthians) instead of just using it to indulge in what he wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:08:20-07:00","id":952060,"title":"","content":"1. He can affored to rent a room, what he doesn't get is the benefit of the Safe Place merit.<br /> 2. A mentor will ask things of their student as covered under the drawback for the merit. It may be the case that the player would be better of replacing the mentor instead of losing his money from time to time.<br /> 3. Sanctity of Merits at the start of the Merits section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:37:28-07:00","id":956382,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the length of the silence. I'm not used to writing on forums and it takes me a while to formulate a post.<br /> <br /> So we had our first session and it went really well. The character in question had an important interaction with his sire who brought him a snack since he was nearly starving (1 blood point). In the end the character lost himself to frenzy and killed the person causing him to lose humanity. The player was a bit disappointed at this lost of humanity but seemed to like very much the fact that it gave him a beat. Also, out of his own initiative he seems to be making alot of efforts to figure out who the girl he killed was and if she has family in order to somehow make amends. (depending on the efforts made i'm inclining on actually giving or rolling for a point of humanity back).<br /> <br /> As for miami in particular. I am wondering in its interactions with miami-beach and wondering on where to end the city's territory (in the kindred sense). I am not used to having so little ... space between cities (i live in Quebec, btw). <br /> So far, i am making miami-beach the territory of the prince where he allows feeding right in accord with deal made with the carthians (essentially anybody who follows the rules can feed there when they want)<br /> <br /> In the next session the characters will be officially introduced to the All-Night Society (i love that term) in an Elysium on a luxury boat belonging to a prominent member of the invictus. <br /> <br /> Concerning the miami nightlife (especially as it pertains to the 80s) do not hesitate if you know things that would add to the feeling of the setting (i've never been to miami tho i've been to florida).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:36:11-07:00","id":956403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/951816-seeking-counsel-for-an-upcoming-game-i-ll-run?p=956382#post956382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we had our first session and it went really well. The character in question had an important interaction with his sire who brought him a snack since he was nearly starving (1 blood point). In the end the character lost himself to frenzy and killed the person causing him to lose humanity. The player was a bit disappointed at this lost of humanity but seemed to like very much the fact that it gave him a beat. Also, out of his own initiative he seems to be making alot of efforts to figure out who the girl he killed was and if she has family in order to somehow make amends. (depending on the efforts made i'm inclining on actually giving or rolling for a point of humanity back).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice twist, were you expecting that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for miami in particular. I am wondering in its interactions with miami-beach and wondering on where to end the city's territory (in the kindred sense). I am not used to having so little ... space between cities (i live in Quebec, btw).<br /> So far, i am making miami-beach the territory of the prince where he allows feeding right in accord with deal made with the carthians (essentially anybody who follows the rules can feed there when they want) </div> </div> </div>Ours was technically the domain of South Florida, encompassing all the mainland south of I-75. The Keys had their own domain, as did Fort Lauderdale, and the farther north you got the smaller and more fractious the domains were. The Everglades and western coast were only lightly controlled, basically being havens for particularly powerful and atavistic vampires. The court of Miami was pretty powerful and at the end the Prince had declared himself King and it was clear he was going to expand further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Concerning the miami nightlife (especially as it pertains to the 80s) do not hesitate if you know things that would add to the feeling of the setting (i've never been to miami tho i've been to florida). </div> </div> </div>There's been a lot of changes between the 80s and now, though Miami Beach has sort of stayed popular, I think at that point development was still working its way outward. You might check out something like Miami Vice, depending on what atmosphere you're going for. Lots of cocaine moved through the area and with it a lot of violent crime. But it helped fuel the big club scene and the money flowed into the city either way. Odds are vampires would have connections with other domains across the Caribbean and Gulf so they could key into that. We had 'ambassadors' who would either travel to and from their own domains or just situate themselves and try to ensure their lines would remain untouched by other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:12:49-07:00","id":956438,"title":"","content":"I was not expecting it at all. I have a strange relationship (tabletopwise) with that player in that he always prefer to dm or storytell than to be a player so i never know what he might do. Case in point, while his reaction towards the victim is one of atonement, his reaction to his sire is one of downright hostility, which i did not expect (tho in retrospect i should have,. I expected a more junkie towards his pusher kind of relation). I did think that eventually he would seek to cut himself from a parasitic sire but the whole killing thing accelerated things much more than i expected. I am a bit scared that a confrontation happens too soon, but all in all i am thrilled with this development. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:18:11-07:00","id":956439,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I forgot about it, but since your game is in the 80s you might check out <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/New_Wave_Requiem\" target=\"_blank\">New Wave Requiem</a>.<br /> <br /> It's always nice when players go deep, though it can be really startling sometimes if you're not prepared for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:24:39-07:00","id":956443,"title":"","content":"Yeah i have, it is a very nice read.<br /> <br /> And so far the funniest thing in the game is that several times i had a player say that he/she wants to call someone and when i ask how he/she goes ''with my cellpho... oh''. I showed them the image of the daeva character in New Wave Requiem at the end of the book, he holds a huge impractical cellphone. We are all old enough to remember a time with no cellphones (or rather not as many) but it still makes for a strange moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}